# Runtime newsletter store. server/services/publishing/store.js creates the
# directory and treats a missing file as an empty list, so nothing here needs
# to exist in the repo - and subscribers.json, imports.json and events.json
# accumulate subscriber email addresses. Tracked, the next `git add -A` puts
# personal data into git history, where removing it means rewriting published
# commits. It was committed once, empty, in #1062 and removed here.
server/data/newsletter/
